Step 1: Create the OIDC provider
- Search EKS > Clusters > your cluster > On Cluster info, copy the OpenID Connect provider URL
- Go to IAM > Identity providers > Add provider
- Choose OpenID Connect, paste the URL as Provider URL, and on Audience enter sts.amazonaws.com > Add Provide

Step 2: Create the IAM role
- Go to IAM > Roles > Create role.
- Choose Web identity, select your OIDC provider, and set Audience to sts.amazonaws.com > Click Next.
- Search for the policy AmazonEBSCSIDriverPolicy > Click Next.
- Name the role AmazonEKS_EBS_CSI_DriverRole and click Create role. (Give any name for role)

Step 3: Install the EBS CSI add-on
- Go to EKS > Clusters > Click on your cluster > Add-ons > Get more add-ons.
- Select Amazon EBS CSI Driver and click Next.
- On Add-on access select IAM roles for service accounts (IRSA)
- On Select IAM roel, select the role you created above i.e, AmazonEKS_EBS_CSI_DriverRole (your role name) and click on Next > Create

#Login to the server which you are using to connect to the cluster and update kubeconfig

- aws eks update-kubeconfig --name=<your-cluster-name> --region=<your-region>

#To check the status
- kubectl get pods -n kube-config